line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</col>
step	189	-	Quick guide step 189
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Climb over the broken fence</col>
step	190	-	Quick guide step 190
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Follow the bloody trail</col>
step	191	-	Quick guide step 191
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Inspect the fence</col>
step	192	-	Quick guide step 192
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</col>
step	193	-	Quick guide step 193
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>When ready, talk to Sugadinti or Ivan to initiate a cutscene.</col>
step	194	-	Quick guide step 194
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, talk to Sugadinti or Ivan to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Once Drakan reaches ~30% (900hp) of his health, the fight will be over.</col>
step	195	-	Quick guide step 195
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, talk to Sugadinti or Ivan to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan reaches ~30% (900hp) of his health, the fight will be over.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Talk to Ivan after the cutscene ends.</col>
step	196	-	Quick guide step 196
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, talk to Sugadinti or Ivan to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan reaches ~30% (900hp) of his health, the fight will be over.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan after the cutscene ends.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Talk to Sugadinti</col>
step	197	-	Quick guide step 197
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, talk to Sugadinti or Ivan to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan reaches ~30% (900hp) of his health, the fight will be over.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan after the cutscene ends.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Travel to the <col=800000>Icyene Graveyard</col></col>
step	198	-	Quick guide step 198
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, talk to Sugadinti or Ivan to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan reaches ~30% (900hp) of his health, the fight will be over.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan after the cutscene ends.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to the Icyene Graveyard</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Talk to Efaritay</col>
step	199	-	Quick guide step 199
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, talk to Sugadinti or Ivan to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan reaches ~30% (900hp) of his health, the fight will be over.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan after the cutscene ends.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to the Icyene Graveyard</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Enter the portal to Vampyrium</col>
step	200	-	Quick guide step 200
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, talk to Sugadinti or Ivan to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan reaches ~30% (900hp) of his health, the fight will be over.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan after the cutscene ends.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to the Icyene Graveyard</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal to Vampyrium</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Gear up at the supply chest on the north wall before starting the fight.</col>
step	201	-	Quick guide step 201
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, talk to Sugadinti or Ivan to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan reaches ~30% (900hp) of his health, the fight will be over.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan after the cutscene ends.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to the Icyene Graveyard</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal to Vampyrium</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up at the supply chest on the north wall before starting the fight.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>The final fight against Drakan has three distinct phases; for a detailed breakdown of the fight, see <col=800000>here</col>.</col>
step	202	-	Quick guide step 202
line	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
line	
line	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
line	
line	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
line	
line	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
line	
line	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
line	
line	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
line	
line	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
line	
line	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
line	
line	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
line	
line	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
line	
line	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
line	
line	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
line	
line	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
line	
line	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
line	
line	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
line	
line	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
line	
line	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
line	
line	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</str>
line	
line	<str>When ready, talk to Sugadinti or Ivan to initiate a cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once Drakan reaches ~30% (900hp) of his health, the fight will be over.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Ivan after the cutscene ends.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sugadinti</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to the Icyene Graveyard</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Efaritay</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the portal to Vampyrium</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear up at the supply chest on the north wall before starting the fight.</str>
line	
line	<str>The final fight against Drakan has three distinct phases; for a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>After defeating Drakan, finish the cutscene to complete the quest.</col>
done	<str>Head to the Icyene Graveyard, accessed via the boat in either southern Burgh de Rott, Meiyerditch, or Slepe. Players can also use the Drakan's medallion teleport to Ver Sinhaza, exit into Meiyerditch, then run to the boat in the south-western corner of the area.</str>
done	
done	<str>Speak to Sarius Guile.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head to the hideout under Old Man Ral's house in Meiyerditch Via the Trap Door Located In the House. (type=maplink|x=3607|y=3208|mtype=pin)</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the nearby chest to obtain a vyre noble outfit if you forgot to bring it.</str>
done	
done	<str>Wear the vyre noble outfit, then inspect the makeshift shrine for a cutscene.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom.</str>
done	
done	<str>Prepare for a fight. The fight is a battle of endurance, you are required to protect yourself and Ivan from multiple vyrewatch and vyrewatch sentinels for several minutes.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Ivan afterwards, and he'll tell you to meet up at the church in Slepe.</str>
done	
done	<str>Travel to Slepe, either via Drakan's medallion teleport to Slepe, or if that is not unlocked, teleport to Ver Sinhaza and run north to Slepe.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Ivan Strom in Slepe, just west of the church.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go into the Slepe pub and ask the bartender Roy about a friend.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the Sisterhood Sanctuary through the stairs south of the church's graveyard.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head north until reaching Kroy's laboratory, then climb the ladder to enter Crombwick Manor.</str>
done	
done	<str>Help Veliaf Hurtz kill the five vyrewatches.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Veliaf.</str>
done	
done	<str>Make your way to Drezel in Paterdomus Temple, which can be quickly reached via fairy ring (CKS).</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Ivan, read the squire's journal, then talk to Ivan again.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head west through the mausoleum and up to the temple, then kill all the monks of Zamorak.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head upstairs and talk to Ivan.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search through the bookcases for six books. Place them books on the plinths in the following order (from north to south):</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Ivan to obtain Ivandis' writings, then read it.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk with him again to return to the mausoleum.</str>
done	
done	<str>Stock up on supplies for a fight with multiple vyrewatches and sentinels.</str>
done	
done	<str>When ready, return to Paterdomus and talk to Ivan or Veliaf.</str>
done	
done	<str>Mine away the blockage immediately south of Ivan. If you do not have a pickaxe, talk to Ivan for a bronze pickaxe.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the blockage and head north-east through the tunnel.</str>
done	
done	<str>There will be a few vyrewatches and vyrewatch sentinels to defeat inside. Focus on the sentinels first while praying protect from magic. They will occasionally spawn a blood orb that will do passive damage.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Ivan.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head north through the entry.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head north-west and climb up either of the stairs.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head east and pray to the shrine to unlock a teleport back here with Drakan's medallion.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the portal at the centre of the room.</str>
done	
done	<str>With (A) as the starting point on the map, Pick up and read the poem scroll on the table just south (B).</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the east door and then search the throne (C), which will reveal four levers in the busts to the east.</str>
done	
done	<str>From north to south, pull the 3rd, 4th, 1st, and 2nd busts in that order</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the throne again for the half moon key.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the south door, then search the shelves (D) to the south-west to find the small clock hand.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the doors to the north, then west, to return to the dining room.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the west door using the half moon key to arrive in a corridor. Walk around the traps to avoid them.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the west door. Quickly search the crate for a tinderbox (E), then climb up the stairs.</str>
done	
done	<str>Take the explosive barrel (F), then enter the south door. Search the crate for a Drakan emblem (G), then exit the room.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the east door, then through the north door.</str>
done	
done	<str>From the uk=1 of the main entrance hall, go through either of the north doors.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the north unmarked door (not the crescent moon door), then head to the south door (next to empty receptacle) while avoiding traps.</str>
done	
done	<str>Place the Drakan emblem on the receptacle (H), then enter. Search the crate in the north-west corner for a large clock hand (I).</str>
done	
done	<str>Exit the room, then return through the western door while avoiding traps.</str>
done	
done	<str>To the east of the crescent moon door is a lever (J); pull it to open a portal.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the portal which will teleport you to (K), then use the south door, then the west door, to return to the dining room fireplace (L)</str>
done	
done	<str>Place the small hand on the western grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 11, and the small hand to 9.</str>
done	
done	<str>Place the large hand on the eastern grandfather clock. Set the big hand to 12, and the small hand to 4.</str>
done	
done	<str>Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a second Drakan emblem.</str>
done	
done	<str>From the chest room (A), go through the west door, then the south-westernmost door to enter a laboratory (B). Kill all the sanguidae.</str>
done	
done	<str>Take the syringe barrel from the table.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the crate to the south-east for a venator stomach.</str>
done	
done	<str>Inspect the sink to the west, and remove the sink plug.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the north-west door (C). Use the sink plug on the sink, then turn the tap on when prompted.</str>
done	
done	<str>Take the broken pipe from the sink. Use it on the nearby cabinet to receive a sharp knife.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the crate near the sink for the syringe plunger.</str>
done	
done	<str>Return to the laboratory (B) through the south door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the sharp knife on the venator corpse to receive a pair of tongs.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the tongs on the sink for a syringe needle. Use one of the syringe parts on another to assemble an empty syringe.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the empty syringe on the venator stomach to receive a full syringe.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the full syringe on the chest to receive a left crest half.</str>
done	
done	<str>From the laboratory, exit through the north-east crescent moon door, then go through the nearest door to return to the main hall.</str>
done	
done	<str>Climb down the stairs (D), then enter the first door on the south side (E). Deal with the venator; pray Protect from Melee or Missiles depending on distance, and turn it off when it is about to screech to avoid damage.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the weapons rack at the east end of the room.</str>
done	
done	<str>The statues must be mirrored on the north and south sides of the rooms. From east to west, they should be holding battleaxes, spears, maces, and swords.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the chest to receive a right crest half. Combine it with the left to create the full crest.</str>
done	
done	<str>Exit the basement through the north-west door, then up the stairs to the west, then from the portal room, go through the doors to the south-east, east, then north.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the full crest on the fireplace. Inspect the fireplace and select "search" to receive a new moon key.</str>
done	
done	<str>From the fireplace, return to the main hall by going through the south, west, then north doors.</str>
done	
done	<str>Climb down the stairs to the basement, then enter the either of the doors on the north side (A) to initiate a cutscene where you free Safalaan and Vanescula.</str>
done	
done	<str>Pick up the gibbous moon key.</str>
done	
done	<str>Leave the jail room through either south door, climb up the stairs to the main hall, then climb up the stairs again to the uk=1.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the south-east door (the gibbous moon door).</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the east, south, then south-east doors. Search the crate for an ornate knife (B).</str>
done	
done	<str>Pull the lever on the western wall. Enter the portal, teleporting to (C). Then go through the north door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the gibbous moon door on the eastern wall. Kill the venator to prevent being disrupted from solving the room puzzle or just run past it.</str>
done	
done	<str>Light the fireplace, then search the chest (D) just east for a lockbox.</str>
done	
done	<str>Open the lockbox with the code (from left to right): the ⠿, the ᴟ, and symbol that looks like ⁘, to get a fancy gem.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the south-west door (E) by inputting the passcode "SPEAR".</str>
done	
done	<str>One of the bookcases (F) will be searchable; do so for a mysterious book.</str>
done	
done	<str>Open the book for another fancy gem, then leave the room.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use both fancy gems on the mounted venator head to the east (G).</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the head for an ornate hourglass, then go through the west door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the ornate skull, hourglass, and knife on the display case to the west (H). The order does not matter.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the display case for a gilded key.</str>
done	
done	<str>From the display case, climb down the staircase, then through the north door - beware of Sanguidae, quickly go through the west door after entering.</str>
done	
done	<str>After this west door (the gilded door), go through the north-west door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Kill the venator in the room, then talk to Ivan.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the northern bookcase for a gilded book.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the south-eastern bookcase for a vampyre book.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the gilded book on the western gilded bookcase, then inspect the books when prompted.</str>
done	
done	<str>Rearrange the symbols of the Vampyric Houses in alphabetical order.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the secret passage to the south. Take the full moon key from the table.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the east door, then the east gilded door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the unmarked north door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the easternmost door, while avoiding the traps.</str>
done	
done	<str>Climb down the stairs, then run west and enter the door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the east full moon door. Kill the webbed-winged crows if necessary.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the north-west shelves and take one of each potion: cloudy grey, weightless black, thick red, and cold bluish-white.</str>
done	
done	<str>Based on the inscriptions on the basin, place the potions in the following basins:</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the altar for an ancient symbol.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the east door, then pull the lever in the north-west corner.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the portal, then go through the south door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the east, east, south-east, then north doors.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the crate by the window for an ancient shield.</str>
done	
done	<str>Combine the shield and symbol to create the shield with symbol.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the south, west, and north doors, then head upstairs.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the south-east (the southern door on the eastern wall) gibbous moon door, then through the south-east full moon door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the shield on the empty mount at the southern wall, then search it for a solid key.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the north and west doors, then go through the east full moon door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the solid door directly across to reach a laboratory.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the shelves to the north-west. Take 2 vials of water, 3 vials of blood, and 3 pure essence.</str>
done	
done	<str>Follow the next steps to place a chemical vial onto the basin until the panel reads 53 HP (haemalchemic potential).</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through the unlocked north door and destroy the blood stockpile.</str>
done	
done	<str>Pick up the crank wheel in the small building 3 houses east of the prayer altar.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go to the building north of the altar and operate the crank base located just outside the house. After you operate the crank, Drakan will start chasing you. Click the crank several times to unlock the door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the house and search the bookshelf for a dusty book, then read it to retrieve the Vitur key.</str>
done	
done	<str>Exit and head to the north-easternmost house with the Vitur door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the shed input the passcode "TOOLS" for a pair of bolt cutters.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head to the building east of the altar to and pick up the tooth half of key from the table.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head to the building directly south of the well (link= map icon). Use the bolt cutters on the chained doors on the north side.</str>
done	
done	<str>Pick up the loop half of key.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the loop and tooth halves together to obtain a Myrmel key.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the Myrmel key to enter the building north-east of the well (link= map icon), and take the Bucket in the back left corner. Use the use Bucket on the well, then go back inside the Myrmel house and use the Bucket of water on the Northern barrel to get the Shadum key.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the Shadum key on the house south-west of Ivan and the group, then pick up the trapdoor key on the crate.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the bank directly south-east of the red fountain to the west and operate the crank (spam click the crank) to open the gate.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the trapdoor to arrive in the house with the altar.</str>
done	
done	<str>Open the chest to the west with the passcode "35158" to receive the Jovkai key.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the house with the Jovkai door (link= map icon) to find the old cog on a crate.</str>
done	
done	<str>Once you leave this house, Drakan will start pursuing the player at running speed, so wait until he is as far from you as possible before rushing back to Ivan and the group. If you teleport out, you'll need to get the old cog again.</str>
done	
done	<str>Take some supplies from Ivan if needed, as you'll be facing Drakan.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Veliaf or Vanescula to initiate a cutscene.</str>
done	
done	<str>After the cutscene, you will be fighting Drakan. You will be assisted by both Vanescula and Veliaf, but don't expect them to deal a lot of damage.</str>
done	
done	<str>Alongside melee attacks, Drakan will frequently use spear lunges that are preceded by a visual cue. The timing of this is precise and so requires tick perfect movements to avoid damage.</str>
done	
done	<str>For a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
done	
done	<str>You must continue dodging his attacks until you are finally able to damage him.</str>
done	
done	<str>Resupply at the tent if needed after your encounter with Drakan. You must use the escape option to access this tent. You can always escape and return here, and you'll respawn in this area if you die.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the west darkwood trees.</str>
done	
done	<str>Two ancient feral vyres will spawn and attack with melee. When fighting multiple of them at once, one will swap places with the other and begin healing, whilst forcing you to attack the vyre that took its place. Simply switch targets to resume attacking the initial vyre.</str>
done	
done	<str>Kill the additional two vyres that spawn, then proceed to the next area.</str>
done	
done	<str>To fell the darkwood trees blocking your path, they must be chopped from two different sides; you may need to jump over the tree stumps multiple times from different sides in order to reach another side of a tree.</str>
done	
done	<str>Chop your way until you reach the north-east corner of the area, from which you can enter the next part of the forest.</str>
done	
done	<str>To avoid the maxilla beasts, you must disable run and walk along the path until you reach the cave. If you are running or are too close to them, they will deal 30-50 damage.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head south-east and enter the cave.</str>
done	
done	<str>Follow the path north and enter the Exit.</str>
done	
done	<str>Waves of nylocas will spawn from two corners. They behave the same way as their Theatre equivalents, becoming immune to attacks if attacked with the wrong style (melee against white, ranged against green), and exploding if left alone long enough.</str>
done	
done	<str>After defeating all the nylocas enter the darkwood trees to the north.</str>
done	
done	<str>Stand behind each of the three blood serpents and "wrangle" them to collect them. Catching them from the front will cause them to attack for 5 poison damage.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use three dead blood serpents on each other to make a serpent rope.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the serpent rope on the long branched tree to the south-east to progress.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then leave the palace via the northern doors and pick amitire leaves from the amitire plant east of the entrance.</str>
done	
done	<str>Return to the palace. Search the shelves next to the sink (south of Efaritay) for a bowl. Fill it with water.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the cupboard by the western wall for a potato and raw impaler meat.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the bowl of water on the potato.</str>
done	
done	<str>Cook the impaler meat at the range, then use the incomplete stew on the cooked meat.</str>
done	
done	<str>Cook the stew, then use the leaves on it to create an amitire stew.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Efaritay, then use the stew on Safalaan.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Efaritay again until you receive some hallowed marks.</str>
done	
done	<str>Free up seven inventory spaces, then head to the east side of the palace.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Ivan or Sarei.</str>
done	
done	<str>Take all three tools from the workbench.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the nearby crates for blisterwood logs and a blessed silver sickle.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the chests in the room for a diamond and an enchant diamond tablet.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the items on the sickle in the following order: diamond, tablet, logs.</str>
done	
done	<str>Create the hallowed flail at the anvil. The blisterwood flail must be present in the inventory.</str>
done	
done	<str>Using a knife on blisterwood logs create blisterwood stakes</str>
done	
done	<str>Make your way downstairs, then talk to Veliaf and then Vanescula. Talk with Veliaf again.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go back upstairs and talk to Sugadinti Vitur</str>
done	
done	<str>Gear up. Take ~15 rancid slimy potions, ~5 foul chunky potions, and 1 rank frothy potion from the supplies table in the base. Combination foods can be helpful, but it can just be easier to spam rancid slimy potions since they do not deplete your stats significantly.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go outside to the bridge to start the defence section.</str>
done	
done	<str>You will need to defend the aranei from the incoming portals with the ballista. The portals will always be one-shot, but they will eventually begin to spawn faster than you can shoot them down.</str>
done	
done	<str>The next defence section requires you to heal aranei and repair the pillars and windows.</str>
done	
done	<str>You will fight off Drakan once again. This time, the aranei and Efaritay will help you, but expect to pull your weight.</str>
done	
done	<str>Alongside the spear lunges from the first encounter, Lowerniel will begin using cleaves that land as a 2x3 AoE in front of and behind him. Efaritay will occasionally heal you and the aranei, and you can always grab more supplies from the supply table if you die.</str>
done	
done	<str>Once Drakan is at 58% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
done	
done	<str>Complete the dialogue at Burgh de Rott after the cutscene.</str>
done	
done	<str>Teleport to Ver Sinhaza using Drakan's medallion.</str>
done	
done	<str>Gear up for a wave based encounter against waves of nylocas, the Maiden of Sugadinti, and the Nylocas Vasilias. It is recommended to bring your strongest melee weapon, as well as fast weapons for each style for ease of completion.</str>
done	
done	<str>The rooms are significantly easier than during A Night at the Theatre, so full gear swaps are not necessary, but can be helpful when fighting the Nylocas Vasilias.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Sugadinti just outside the notice board to begin the encounter.</str>
done	
done	<str>Make your way to Burgh de Rott. Gear up for a melee-based fight with the hallowed flail.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head to the ruined building to the north-east to find Ivan and Veliaf. (type=maplink|x=3543|y=3258|mtype=pin)</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Veliaf and enter the nearby entry</str>
done	
done	<str>You will fight the wyrd. He will knock back the player with every punch, so ensure there is space behind you.</str>
done	
done	<str>The wyrd attacks in a repeating cycle with 2 melee attacks, a screech, another 2 melee attacks, another screech, then a double slam. This cycle repeats until around 60% health, where he will sometimes use a bloody screech in place of a regular screech. See the clips below for a demonstration.</str>
done	
done	<str>Once the wyrd is at 10% health, a cutscene will play.</str>
done	
done	<str>Climb over the broken fence</str>
done	
done	<str>Follow the bloody trail</str>
done	
done	<str>Inspect the fence</str>
done	
done	<str>Exit the Burgh de Rott hideout and gear up at the bank for another fight against Drakan.</str>
done	
done	<str>When ready, talk to Sugadinti or Ivan to initiate a cutscene.</str>
done	
done	<str>Once Drakan reaches ~30% (900hp) of his health, the fight will be over.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Ivan after the cutscene ends.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Sugadinti</str>
done	
done	<str>Travel to the Icyene Graveyard</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Efaritay</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the portal to Vampyrium</str>
done	
done	<str>Gear up at the supply chest on the north wall before starting the fight.</str>
done	
done	<str>The final fight against Drakan has three distinct phases; for a detailed breakdown of the fight, see here.</str>
done	
done	<str>After defeating Drakan, finish the cutscene to complete the quest.</str>
done	
done	<col=ff0000>QUEST COMPLETE!</col>
